<clickhouse>
    <!-- Spill heavy aggregations and sorts to disk instead of failing in RAM.

         Root cause, 2026-10-17. The Langfuse web service kept answering with
         "Your query could not be completed... Request timed out", and every one of
         those was the same ClickHouse exception underneath:

             Code: 241. DB::Exception: (total) memory limit exceeded:
             would use 3.22 GiB (attempt to allocate chunk of 4.16 MiB)

         against a 4 GB server cap set in `memory.xml`. ClickHouse's external
         memory settings default to 0, which DISABLES them: a GROUP BY or ORDER BY
         is executed in RAM and either fits or dies. So the cap was doing its job
         and the query had no second option. The API then reported the death as a
         timeout, which reads like a network or upstream problem and sent the
         investigation at the wrong layer for an hour.

         The box has 21 GB of free disk, so letting these queries spill is the
         honest fix. The alternative — giving ClickHouse a larger slice of a 7.9 GB
         VM shared with ClickHouse, Redis, MinIO, the worker and the Cloud SQL
         proxy — buys a bigger ceiling without removing the failure.

         MOUNTED AT `users.d`, NOT `config.d`. These are profile settings, and the
         image's `users.xml` ships its own `<profiles><default>` block. At config.d
         the values were accepted at startup and `system.settings` still reported 0
         — the mount looked right and did nothing. This file's location in the repo
         is unchanged; only the mount target differs.

         1 GB per operator sits well below the 4 GB server cap and well above the
         working set of an ordinary query, so the thresholds only bite on the
         pathological queries, which are precisely the ones that were dying. -->
    <profiles>
        <default>
            <max_bytes_before_external_group_by>1000000000</max_bytes_before_external_group_by>
            <max_bytes_before_external_sort>1000000000</max_bytes_before_external_sort>
        </default>
    </profiles>
</clickhouse>
